MLLM description: The Horned Grebe is a small to medium-sized waterbird with a distinctive crest of feathers on its head, which is most prominent in breeding plumage. Its body is covered in dark brown or black plumage, with lighter underparts and a white patch on the chest. The bill is short and pointed, and the legs are short and set far back on the body, giving it an awkward appearance when walking on land. The Horned Grebe is often seen swimming on the surface of the water, diving for food, and preening itself. It is a strong swimmer and can remain underwater for up to two minutes. The Horned Grebe is also known for its elaborate courtship display, which involves the male performing a series of dives and surface runs while making loud calls.
